BalanceNG 3.134 is now available at http://www.BalanceNG.net
Release-Date: August 18, 2010

----

Changes:

* The BalanceNG agent ("bngagent") has been rewritten fixing several IPv6 related bugs.

* The directive "target N agent6" has been implemented now supporting agent communication over UDP/IPv6.

* The manual has been updated accordingly.

----

Here's the newest online example explaining IPv6 SLB (Server Load-
Balancing) in DSR mode with BalanceNG V3: http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example11.html

----

About BalanceNG:

BalanceNG is a software load-balancer and runs on Linux and Solaris operating systems. BalanceNG is the core load-balancing engine of the SECUDOS and Thomas-Krenn load-balancer appliances.

About Inlab Software GmbH:

Inlab Software GmbH, founded in 1991 is an ISV (Independent Software Vendor) located in Gruenwald near Munich, Germany. Inlab focuses on networking system software, load-balancing software, programming languages and security software. Inlab develops software for Linux and Solaris operating systems and develops both commercial products and Open-Source software.

----

Best Regards,
Thomas Obermair
Inlab Software GmbH

----

OEM-Partner BalanceNG certified systems:

* Available Worldwide:
  The SECUDOS Load-Balancer (SLB) Product Family
  http://www.secudos.com/metadot/index.pl?id=4703;isa=Category;op=show

* Available in Europe:
  Thomas-Krenn LoadBalancer (TKLB)
  http://www.thomas-krenn.com/en/further-areas/load-balancer.html

